hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"8746","Ibrahim ibn al-Hasan told me, on the authority of Hajjaj. Ibn Jurayj said: Sulayman al-Ahwal informed me, that he heard Amr ibn Dinar, asking his father Salama bin Abdul Rahman, about women’s isolation, and he said: Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri claimed that a man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Oh Prophet of God, I have a female slave, and I isolate her, and I do not isolate her except out of fear of the child. The Jews claimed that she was the youngest servant, so he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “The Jews have lied, the Jews have lied.” So I asked Abu Salamah: Did you hear it from Abu Sa`id? He said: No, but a man told me about him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8747","Al-Haytham bin Ayyub Al-Talqani told me, he said: Ibrahim bin Saad told me, he said: Ibn Shihab told me, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about isolation, and he said: “You do not have to do it, for there is no A breath that is destined to come into being, but it is.” Hamza said: It is a mistake"
"8748","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Abdul Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about isolation. He said: “Or will you do it?” They said: Yes. He said: “Then you do not have to do it.” Do so, for God has not decreed for any soul to create it unless it exists.” Hamza said: This is also a mistake. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8749","Kathir ibn Ubaid al-Humsi told us, he said: Muhammad ibn Harb told us, on the authority of al-Zubaidi, and he is Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Humsi, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ibn Muhayriz, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, that they asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about isolation. He said: “You do not have to You do it. There is not a breath that God has written in the heart of a servant but it will emanate until the Day of Resurrection.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8750","Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Azeem told us, he said: Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Asma told us, he said: Juwayriyah bin Asma told us, on the authority of Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhayriz, a Syrian, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, who said: We were captured as captives, and we were isolated, then We asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about that, and he said to us: “You will do it, and you will do it? There is not a single breeze that comes to me.” On the Day of Resurrection, it will exist.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: The hadith of Malik, and al-Zubaidi is more likely to be correct. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8751","Harun bin Abdullah told me, he said: Ibn Abi Fudaik, on the authority of Al-Dahhak bin Uthman, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, on the authority of Ibn Muhayriz, that he heard Abu Sarmah and Abu Sa`id al-Khudri say: We were captured as captives in the battle of al-Mustaliq, which is the battle In which the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, injured Juwayriyah, and among us were those who wanted to take a family, and among us were those who wanted to enjoy And he sold, so we decided to isolate, so we mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “You do not have to isolate, for God has He who is a creator is destined until the Day of Resurrection.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8752","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Qaza’ah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id He said: Isolation was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Why would any of you do that?” And he did not say: He will not do that. One of you is that, “There is no created soul except Allah, its Creator.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8753","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Omar told us, and he is the son of Abi Khalifa, he said: Muhammad bin Amr told us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was asked about isolation, and it was said: O Messenger of God, the Jews claim that she is the youngest Mawaddah. He said: “The Jews lied.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8754","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: “We were We do it according to the covenant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace,” meaning isolation. I said to Amr: Did you hear it from Jabir? He said: No (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8755","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Jabir, he said: “We used to isolate during the reign of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, and the Qur’an is being revealed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8756","Humayd bin Masada told us, on the authority of Bishr, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Bishr al-Ansari, He said: He rejected the hadith, until he referred it to Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, who said: This was mentioned to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “And what “Is that?” They said: A man has a woman, and she breastfeeds for him, and he becomes infected with her, and he hates for her to become pregnant by him, and for him to be a slave girl. So he gets pregnant from her, and he hates for her to become pregnant from him. He said: So he said: “You do not have to do that, for it is the destiny.”"
"8757","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Hassan Al-Makhzoumi, on the authority of Urwa bin Ayadh, on the authority of Jabir bin Abd God, he said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: I have a slave girl, and I am isolated from her, so he said: “But that does not prevent anything.” God willed. Then he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “Did you feel that that slave girl had become pregnant?” He said: “I am the servant of God and His Messenger!” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8758","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Thabit told us, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Jews were, When a woman among them menstruates, they shall not eat with her, nor drink with her, nor have intercourse with her in the houses. Then God Almighty revealed: And they ask you about Menstruation Say: It is a harm, so keep away from menstruating women and do not approach them until they are purified. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do all \Nothing"","" except intercourse.\"""""""
"8759","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Muhammad bin Jafar, he said: Shu`bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid bin Abd al-Rahman. Ibn Zayd Ibn Al-Khattab, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, regarding one who has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating, he said “He gives in charity a dinar, or half a dinar.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8760","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told us, he said: Saeed bin Amir told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abdul Hamid, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, regarding the one who has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating, said: “He should give in charity a dinar, or half a dinar.” Shu'bah said: As for my memory, it is raised, and so-and-so and so-and-so said: He was not raising it. Some of the people said: O Abu Bastam, tell us about your memory. We said goodbye to so-and-so, and he said: By God, I do not like that I spoke of this and remained silent about this, and that I lived in this world as long as Noah lived among his people."
"8761","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Zaafrani told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Sabbah, he said: Ismail bin Zakaria told us, on the authority of, then he mentioned Amr bin Qais, On the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “A man had intercourse with his wife while she was menstruating, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded him to He gives half a dinar in charity.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8762","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Abu Abdullah Al-Shaqri, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of a man He had intercourse with his wife while she was menstruating. He said: “He should give in charity a dinar, or half a dinar.”"
"8763","Wasil bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Asbat bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in A man has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating. He said: “He gives a dinar or half a dinar in charity.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8764","Abu Asim Khushish bin Asram Al-Nasa’i told us, he said: We are Rawh, and Abdullah bin Bakr, they said: We are Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of Qatada, On the authority of Abdul Hamid, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that “a man had intercourse with his wife while she was menstruating, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded him to do so.” To give in charity a dinar, or half a dinar.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8765","Harun bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Abdah, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “He commanded a man who had an intercourse with his wife while she was menstruating to give a dinar or half a dinar in charity.” Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Asim bin Hilal told us, he said: Qatada told us, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, with something similar, but he did not narrate it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8766","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Sufyan bin Uyaynah, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Muqasim, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, regarding one who has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating, he said: “If the blood is foul, then a dinar, and if there is yellowness in it, then half a dinar.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8767","Muhammad bin Kamil Al-Marwazi told us, saying: I am Hushaym, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Miqasam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about a man having intercourse with his wife while she was menstruating. He said: “He gives half a dinar in charity.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: 5 Hajjaj ibn Artaat is weak and accustomed to deception 5 (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8768","Yusuf bin Saeed bin Muslim Al-Masisi told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Khusayf told me, on the authority of Maqsim, He told him that Ibn Abbas told him that a man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and had sexual intercourse with his wife while she was menstruating. So he ordered him \For half a dinar\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"8769","Hilal bin Al-Ala told me, he said: Husayn told me, he said: Abu Khaythamah told me, he said: Khusayf told me, on the authority of Miqsam, he said: “When a man fell on His wife, who was menstruating, was ordered by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to give him half a dinar, which he should give in charity.”"
"8770","Muhammad bin Ali bin Maimun told us, he said: Al-Faryabi told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Miqsam, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: May God bless him and grant him peace regarding what is committed on his wife while she is menstruating: “He should give half a dinar in charity.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8771","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Abd al-Razzaq, he said: we are Muammar, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “If If she is menstruating, give him a dinar in charity. “And Miqsam said: If she is menstruating after she is pure, then half a dinar, as long as she does not wash.”"
"8772","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: I am a partner, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in a man who fell on his wife while she was menstruating, “so he ordered him to give half a dinar in charity.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8773","Sahl bin Salih Al-Antaki told us, he said: Muhammad bin Issa is Ibn Al-Tabbaa’, he said: I am a partner, on the authority of Khusayf, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, regarding a woman who has intercourse with her family while she is menstruating, he said: “He should give in charity half a dinar.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8774","Ahmad ibn Harb told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in the man He had intercourse with his wife while she was menstruating. He said: “If he had intercourse with foul blood, he should give a dinar in charity, and if it was yellow, then half a dinar.”"
"8775","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Tamim told us, he said: Musa bin Ayyub told us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Muslim, on the authority of Ibn Jabir, on the authority of Ali bin Dhimah, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that a man told the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he had hurt his wife, While she was menstruating, he ordered him to free Nasma. Mahmoud bin Khalid disagreed with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8776","Mahmoud bin Khalid told me, he said: Al-Walid told me, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid al-Sulami, he said: I heard Ali bin Dhimah, saying: I heard Saeed bin Jubayr, saying: I heard Ibn Abbas, saying: A man said: O Messenger of God, I have intercourse with my wife, and she is menstruating, so he ordered him The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “to free Nasma.” Ibn Abbas said: The value of a breeze at that time was a dinar."
"8777","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Al-Mu’tamir told us, he said: I read to Fudayl, on the authority of Abu Hariz, that Ayfa’ narrated to him, that he asked Saeed bin Jubayr, about the one who broke the fast in Ramadan, said: Ibn Abbas used to say: “Whoever breaks the fast in Ramadan, he must free a slave, or fast.” a month, or feeding thirty poor people.” I said: And whoever has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating, or hears the Friday call to prayer, and does not perform it, does not have the right to An excuse. He said: “Likewise, freeing a slave.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: 5 Abu Hariz is weak in hadith, 5 and I do not know him. Hamza said: Abu Hariz Abdullah bin Al Hussein is a judge. Two syllables (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8778","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Mansour, he said: I heard Ibrahim, he said: He did not mention It contains the lions, and when the last time he mentioned it, on the authority of the lions, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was “commanding “One of us is wearing her robe while she is menstruating, then he has intercourse with her,” and he may have said: “he has intercourse with her.”"
"8779","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, in his hadith, on the authority of Khalid bin Al-Harith, he said: Shu’bah told me, he said: Al-Miqdam told me, he said: I heard my father talking, that he heard Aisha say: “I was drinking while I was menstruating, then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, would take it and put it in his mouth.” On the place where I drank and was sweating, then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, took it and put his mouth on that place.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8780","Abd al-Rahman bin Khalid told me, he said: Harith bin Atiya, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: A messenger came out God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw a woman, so he returned and went to Zainab and fulfilled his needs, then he went out to his companions and said: “Indeed A woman comes in the form of a devil, and backs away in the form of a devil. Whoever among you sees any of that, let him go to her family, for That is a reward for him.” Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Harb, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sitting, and a woman passed by him. He liked it.” He changed it to “the image of a devil,” and did not mention what came after it. This is as if it was more correct than the one before it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8781","Kathir bin Ubaid Al-Humsi told us, he said: Muhammad bin Harb, on the authority of Al-Zubaidi, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, that Umm Kulthum bint Uqba told him that she heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “The one who makes peace between people is not a liar. So he says: good, or he promotes good, and he did not permit anything that people say is a lie except in three: war, reconciliation between people, and hadith. “A man is his wife, and a woman’s speech is her husband.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8782","Abu Salih Muhammad bin Zanbour Al-Makki told us, he said: We are Ibn Abi Hazim, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abdul Wahhab bin Abu Bakr, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his mother Umm Kulthum bint Uqba, that she heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace God, may God bless him and grant him peace, does not permit any lying except in three cases. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: “I do not consider it a lie: a man reconciles between People say things that they want to do right, and a man says something about war, and a man talks to his wife, and a woman talks to her husband.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8783","Ahmad bin Amr bin Al-Sarh told us, he said: I am Ibn Wahb, he said: Iyadh bin Abdullah Al-Qurashi told me, and another mentioned, on the authority of my father Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, Umm Kulthum told me, on the authority of Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that a man asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Peace and blessings of God be upon him, on the authority of a man who has intercourse with his wife, then becomes lazy. Does he have to wash himself? Aisha was sitting, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I will do that, me and her, then we will take a bath.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8784","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Walid told us, he said: I heard Al-Awza’i, saying: Abdul Rahman bin Al-Qasim told me, he said: He told me Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha, said: “If circumcision has passed, then washing is required, and I and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did it.” He greeted us and we bathed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8785","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Waki’ narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to order me to cover myself while I was menstruating, and he would have intercourse with me.”"
"8786","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Abu Al-Nadr, on the authority of Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Al-Thawri, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, On the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to consult me while he was fasting, but he used to control you for his sake.”"
"8787","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: I said to Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim: I heard your father telling, on the authority of Aisha, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to kiss her while he was fasting”? I was silent for an hour, then he said: Yes"
"8788","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Prophet May God bless him and grant him peace, to kiss me. I said: I am fasting. He said: I am fasting. So he kissed me. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8789","Al-Hussein bin Harith told us, he said: I am Jarir, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Shabi, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace: “He continues to fast and kisses whatever he wants from my face.”"
"8790","Ziyad bin Ayyub told me, he said: Ibn Abi Zaida told me, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Salih al-Asadi, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Ash’ath ibn Qais, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would not refrain from anything before me while he was fasting.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8791","Kathir ibn Ubaid informed us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Harb, on the authority of Al-Zubaidi, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “The women of Quraysh are the best women to ride camels, take care of a child, and take care of a husband at the same time.” \His hand.\"" Abu Hurairah said: Maryam bint Imran never rode a camel. (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"8792","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Muhammad bin Mahboub told us, he said: Sarar bin Mujjar bin Qabisah al-Basri told us, trustworthy 5, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Orouba, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “God does not look at a woman who is not grateful to her husband, and she cannot do without him.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: 5 This is Sarrar ibn Majshar, trustworthy, 5 Basri, he and Yazid ibn Zurayi are mentioned in the name of Sa`id ibn Abi Arouba. Because Saeed changed at the end of his life, so whoever heard from him in the past, his hadith is authentic. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8793","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Al-Khalil bin Omar bin Ibrahim told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Amr said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God does not look at a woman who is not grateful to her husband.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8794","'Ali ibn Hajar ibn Iyas informed us, he said: 'Isa ibn Yunus informed us, he said: Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us, from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Urwah, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah, she said: Eleven women sat together and pledged and covenanted that they would not conceal anything from each other about the affairs of their husbands. The first said: \My husband is lean camel meat"","" atop a mountain—neither easy to ascend to"","" nor fat to be carried away.\"" The second said: \""My husband—I will not spread his news"","" for I fear I would not spare him. If I mention him"","" I mention his defects and his faults.\"" The third said: \""My husband is al-'Ashannaq (the tall"","" thin one). If I speak"","" I am divorced"","" and if I am silent"","" I am suspended.\"" The fourth said: \""My husband is like the night of Tihamah—neither hot"","" nor cold"","" nor fear"","" nor weariness.\"" The fifth said: \""My husband"","" when he enters"","" he is gentle (like a fawn)"","" and when he goes out"","" he is fierce (like a lion)"","" and he does not ask about what he has left behind.\"" The sixth said: \""My husband"","" when he eats"","" he wraps up; when he drinks"","" he sucks; when he lies down"","" he coils up; and he does not insert his hand to know the distress.\"" The seventh said: \""My husband is 'ayaya' or 'ghayaya' (a blockhead"","" dull-witted)—every disease has a disease (cure) of its own. He may strike you"","" or break your limb"","" or do both to you.\"" The eighth said: \""My husband—the touch is the touch of a hare"","" and the scent is the scent of a Zarnab (a fragrant plant).\"" The ninth said: \""My husband is lofty in status"","" long in sword-strap"","" great in ashes (i.e."","" generous in cooking)"","" and his house is near the gathering place.\"" The tenth said: \""My husband is Malik. And what is Malik? Malik is better than that. He has many camels"","" abundant in grazing"","" few in pasturing. When they hear the sound of the mizhar (a musical instrument)"","" they are certain they are doomed.\"" The eleventh said: \""My husband is Abu Zar'. And what is Abu Zar'? He adorned my ears with jewellery and filled my arms with fat. He delighted me"","" and my soul delighted in me. He found me among the people of a small flock in a barren place"","" and placed me among the people of neighing (horses)"","" braying (mules)"","" treading (cattle)"","" and threshing (grain). With him I speak and am not rebuked"","" I sleep and wake refreshed"","" and I drink and quench my thirst. The mother of Abu Zar'—and what is the mother of Abu Zar'? Her burdens are heavy"","" and her house is spacious. The son of Abu Zar'—and what is the son of Abu Zar'? His bed is like the branch of a palm"","" and the arm of the young she-camel satisfies him. The daughter of Abu Zar'—and what is the daughter of Abu Zar'? She is obedient to her father and obedient to her mother"","" her garment is full"","" and her maid is enraged. The maid of Abu Zar'—and what is the maid of Abu Zar'? She does not spread our conversation"","" nor does she squander our provisions"","" nor does she fill our house with rubbish.\"" She said: Abu Zar' went out while the milk-skins were being churned"","" and he met a woman with two children like two leopards"","" playing beneath her waist with two pomegranates. He divorced me and married her. After him I married a noble young man"","" who rode a fine horse"","" took a generous share"","" and brought me abundant livestock. He gave me a pair from every kind of animal and said: \""Eat"","" O Mother of Umm Zar'"","" and provision your family.\"" She said: Even if I gathered everything he gave me"","" it would not fill the smallest vessel of Abu Zar'. 'A'ishah said: The Messenger of Allah"","" peace be upon him"","" said to me: \""I was to you as Abu Zar' was to Umm Zar'.\"""""""
"8795","Abu 'Uqbah Khalid ibn 'Uqbah ibn Khalid al-Sakuni al-Kufi informed us, he said: My father 'Uqbah ibn Khalid related to me, he said: Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from 'A'ishah, she said: Eleven women gathered in the pre-Islamic era and pledged to be sincere with one another and not to conceal anything from each other about the affairs of their husbands. The first said: \My husband is lean camel meat"","" atop a mountain—neither fat to be ascended to"","" nor easy to be carried away.\"" The second said: \""My husband—I will not spread his news"","" for I fear I would not spare him. If I mention him"","" I mention his defects and his faults.\"" The third said: \""My husband is al-'Ashannaq. If I speak"","" I am divorced"","" and if I am silent"","" I am suspended.\"" The fourth said: \""My husband is like the night of Tihamah—neither hot"","" nor cold"","" nor fear"","" nor weariness.\"" The fifth said: \""My husband"","" when he enters"","" he is gentle"","" and when he goes out"","" he is fierce"","" and he does not ask about what he has left behind.\"" The sixth said: \""My husband"","" when he eats"","" he wraps up; when he drinks"","" he sucks; when he sleeps"","" he coils up; and he does not insert his hand to know the distress.\"" The seventh said: \""My husband is 'ayaya'—every disease has a disease of its own. He may strike you"","" or break your limb"","" or do both to you.\"" The eighth said: \""My husband is lofty in status"","" long in sword-strap"","" great in ashes"","" and his house is near the gathering place.\"" The ninth said: \""My husband—the touch is the touch of a hare"","" and the scent is the scent of a Zarnab. I overpower him"","" and the people overpower him.\"" The tenth said: \""My husband is Malik. And what is Malik? Malik is better than that. He has many camels"","" abundant in grazing"","" few in pasturing. When they hear the sound of the mizhar"","" they are certain they are doomed.\"" The eleventh said: \""My husband is Abu Zar'. And what is Abu Zar'? He adorned my ears with jewellery and filled my arms with fat. He delighted me"","" and my soul delighted in me. He found me among the people of a small flock in a barren place"","" and placed me among the people of neighing"","" braying"","" treading"","" and threshing. With him I speak and am not rebuked"","" I drink and quench my thirst"","" and I sleep and wake refreshed. The mother of Abu Zar'—and what is the mother of Abu Zar'? Her burdens are heavy"","" and her house is spacious. The son of Abu Zar'—and what is the son of Abu Zar'? His bed is like the branch of a palm"","" and the arm of the young she-camel satisfies him. The daughter of Abu Zar'—and what is the daughter of Abu Zar'? She is obedient to her father and obedient to her mother"","" her garment is empty"","" and her wrapper is full"","" and her maid is enraged. The maid of Abu Zar'—and what is the maid of Abu Zar'? She does not spread our conversation"","" nor does she deceive our provisions"","" nor does she fill our house with rubbish.\"" Abu Zar' went out from me while the milk-skins were being churned"","" and he met a woman with two children like two leopards"","" playing beneath her waist with two pomegranates. Abu Zar' married her and divorced me. After him I married a noble young man"","" who rode a fine horse"","" took a generous share"","" and brought me abundant livestock. He said: \""Eat"","" and provision your family.\"" Even if I gathered everything he gave me"","" it would not fill a vessel from among the vessels of Abu Zar'. 'A'ishah said: The Messenger of Allah"","" peace be upon him"","" said to me: \""I was to you as Abu Zar' was to Umm Zar'.\"" Hisham said: Yazid ibn Roman related to me"","" from 'Urwah"","" from 'A'ishah"","" from the Prophet"","" peace be upon him"","" the like of that"","" meaning the end of the hadith."""""
"8796","Abdul Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam told us, he said: Rayhan bin Saeed bin Al-Muthanna Abu Asmah told us, he said: Abbad bin Mansour told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: O Aisha, I was to you like the father of Zar’a to the mother of Zar’a.” Aisha said: May my father and mother be sacrificed, O Messenger of God. Who was the father of Zar’a? He said: “Ten people gathered together.” Women, so they swore to tell the truth on behalf of their husbands, and one of them said: I will not tell anything about him, I fear that I will not protect him from harm.” Its length, and at the end he said: Then Aisha said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of God. Rather, you are better to me than Abu Zar’. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8797","Ibrahim ibn Ya'qub informed me, he said: 'Abd al-Malik ibn Ibrahim—in the year two hundred and three—dictated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Muhammad Abu Nafi' informed us, he said: Al-Qasim ibn 'Abd al-Wahid related to me, he said: 'Umar ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Urwah related to me, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah, she said: I boasted of my father's wealth in the pre-Islamic era, and it had amounted to a thousand awqiyyah. The Prophet, peace be upon him, said: \Be silent"","" O 'A'ishah"","" for I was to you as Abu Zar' was to Umm Zar'.\"" Then the Messenger of Allah"","" peace be upon him"","" began to narrate to him: \""Indeed"","" eleven women gathered in the pre-Islamic era and pledged that each woman would inform about what was in her husband and not lie.\"" It was said: \""You"","" O so-and-so.\"" She said: \""The night is the night of Tihamah—neither hot"","" nor cold"","" nor fear.\"" It was said: \""You"","" O so-and-so.\"" She said: \""The scent is the scent of the Zarnab"","" and the touch is the touch of a hare. I overpower him"","" and the people overpower him.\"" It was said: \""You"","" O so-and-so.\"" She said: \""By Allah"","" I know nothing—he is indeed lofty in status"","" long in sword-strap"","" great in ashes"","" and his house is near the gathering place.\"" It was said: \""You"","" O so-and-so.\"" She said: \""I married Malik. And what is Malik? He has many camels"","" abundant in pasturing"","" few in grazing. When they hear the sound of the mizhar"","" they are certain they are doomed.\"" It was said: \""You"","" O so-and-so.\"" She said: \""Leave me"","" I will not mention him. If I mention him"","" I mention his defects and his faults. I fear I would not spare him.\"" It was said: \""You"","" O so-and-so.\"" She said: \""Lean camel meat"","" on a mountain—neither fat to be ascended to"","" nor easy to be carried away.\"" It was said: \""You"","" O so-and-so.\"" She said: \""By Allah"","" I know nothing—when he enters"","" he is gentle"","" and when he goes out"","" he is fierce.\"" It was said: \""You"","" O so-and-so.\"" She said: \""By Allah"","" I know nothing—when he eats"","" he devours; when he drinks"","" he sucks; when he slaughters"","" he tears; when he sleeps"","" he coils up; and he does not insert his hand to know the distress.\"" It was said: \""You"","" O so-and-so.\"" She said: \""I married al-'Ashannaq. If I am silent"","" I am suspended"","" and if I speak"","" I am divorced.\"" It was said: \""You"","" O so-and-so.\"" She said: \""'Ayaya'—every disease has a disease of its own. He may strike you"","" or break your limb"","" or do both to you.\"" It was said: \""You"","" O so-and-so.\"" She said: \""I married Abu Zar'. And what is Abu Zar'? He adorned my ears"","" and brought forth from the fat of my arms. He delighted my soul"","" and it delighted in me. He found me among a small flock in a barren place"","" and placed me among the people of camels"","" neighing horses"","" braying mules"","" treading cattle"","" and threshing grain. With him I sleep and wake refreshed"","" I drink and quench my thirst"","" and I speak and am not rebuked. The son of Abu Zar'—and what is the son of Abu Zar'? His bed is like the branch of a palm"","" and the arm of the young she-camel satisfies him. The daughter of Abu Zar'—and what is the daughter of Abu Zar'? Her wrapper is full"","" her garment empty"","" the beauty of her father"","" the beauty of her mother"","" and the vexation of her maid. The maid of Abu Zar'—and what is the maid of Abu Zar'? She does not spread our conversation as gossip"","" nor does she squander our provisions as waste.\"" He went out from me while the milk-skins were being churned"","" and lo"","" there was a woman with two boys like two falcons. Abu Zar' married her and divorced me. I exchanged"","" and every exchange was defective. I married a noble young man"","" who rode a fine horse"","" took a generous share"","" and gave me abundant livestock. He gave me a pair from every grazing animal and said: \""Provision yourself with this"","" O Mother of Umm Zar'"","" and provision your family.\"" I gathered all of that"","" and it did not fill the smallest vessel from among the vessels of Abu Zar'. 'A'ishah said: I said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" rather you are better than Abu Zar'.\"""""""
"8798","Hilal bin Al-Alaa told me, he said: Our father, he said: Khalaf is the son of Khalifa, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Abd God Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Shall I not inform you about your wives from the people of Paradise? On her husband, who, when she hurts or is harmed, comes until she takes her husband’s hand, then says: By God, I will not taste bitterness until she is satisfied.”"
"8799","Al-Qasim bin Zakaria bin Dinar Al-Kufi told us, he said: Husayn bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Maysarah Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Abu Hazim, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Take care of women, for women were created from a rib, even if it is crooked.” “Something in the rib at the top, if you go to straighten it, you will break it, and if you leave it, it will remain crooked, so be kind to women.”"
"8800","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Abu Nu’aym told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muharib bin Dathar, on the authority of Jabir, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade May God bless him and grant him peace, for a man to go to his family at night, to betray them, or to seek out their faults.”"
"8801","Muhammad ibn Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, on the authority of Jabir, he said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade “Peace be upon him, if a man has been absent for a long time, he must come to his family on his way.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8802","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Asim al-Ahwal, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Jabir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He, peace and blessings be upon him: “When one of you comes from his journey, he should not go to his family at night.”"
"8803","Al-Hasan bin Ismail bin Suleiman told us, he said: I am Hushaym, on the authority of Sayyar, on the authority of Al-Shabi, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: We were with The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was on a journey, and when we returned we went to enter. He said: “Give it some time until we enter at night,” meaning: dinner, until you have your hair. \The Sha'atha"","" and the disappearance is getting worse\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"8804","Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Al-Hakam told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Sayyar, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, on the authority of Jabir. Ibn Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you enter at night, do not let your family enter until sunset is ready. And the hair is combed, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When you enter, you must wear a sack.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8805","Harun bin Abdullah told us, he said: Yazid bin Harun told us, he said: I am Hammam bin Yahya, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, on the authority of Anas, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “did not go to his family at night; he would come in the morning or in the evening.”"
"8806","Muhammad bin Muawiyah bin Malij told us, he said: A successor, who is Ibn Khalifa, told us, on the authority of Hafs bin Akhi Anas bin Malik, on the authority of Anas, he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is not appropriate for a human being to prostrate to another human being. And if it were appropriate for a human being to prostrate to another human being, I would command A woman is to prostrate to her husband, out of his great right over her.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8807","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Abu Ahmad told us, he said: Mas’ar told us, on the authority of Abu Ataba, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace: Which people have the greatest right over a woman? He said: “Her husband.” I said: Which people have the greatest right over a man? He said: “His mother.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8808","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: I am Yahya, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, he said: Saeed bin Abi Saeed told me, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “O God, I grant the rights of the weak: the orphan and the woman.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8809","Ahmad ibn Bakkar told us, he said: Ours is Muhammad, and he is Ibn Salamah, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Al-Maqbari, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Shurayh Al-Khuza’i, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Oh God, I make the rights of the weak vulnerable: the rights of the orphan and the rights of women.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8810","Hussein bin Mansour bin Jaafar told me, he said: Mubashir bin Abdullah told me, he said: Sufyan bin Hussein told us, on the authority of Daoud al-Warraq. It was said: He is Ibn Abi Hind, on the authority of Saeed bin Hakim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather Muawiyah. He said: I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and when I was pushed to him and said: By God who sent you, did he send you with what you say? He said: “Yes.” He said: He commanded you to do what you command us. He said: “Yes.” He said: “So what do you say about our women?” He said: “They are your land, so come to your land wherever you wish, and feed them with what you eat, and clothe them with what you clothe, and do not beat them.” “And do not make them ugly.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8811","Al-Hussein bin Harith informed us, saying: I am Ibn Ulayya, on the authority of Saeed Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Al-Saleel, on the authority of Nu’aym ibn Qanab, that Abu Dharr, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Woman was created from a rib, so if you go to straighten her, you will break her, and if you leave her, you will break her.” For therein is a period of time and relief.”"
"8812","Imran bin Musa told us, he said: Abdul-Warith told us, he said: Suleiman al-Taymi told us, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Osama, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “I have not left behind me a trial more harmful to men than women.”"
"8813","Harun bin Ishaq told us, he said: Hafs, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him, then he mentioned a word that means: “The most perfect of believers in faith is the one with the best character, and the kindest to his family.”"
"8814","Abdah bin Abd al-Rahim al-Marwazi told me, he said: This is Amr bin Muhammad, meaning Al-Anqazi, he said: I am Yunus bin Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Aizar bin Harith, on the authority of Al-Numan bin Bashir, who said: Abu Bakr asked permission to come to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he heard Aisha’s loud voice. She said: By God, I know that Ali is more beloved to you than my father. Then Abu Bakr leaned towards her to slap her, and said: O daughter of so-and-so, I see you raising your voice against the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, seized him, and Abu Bakr left angry. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Aisha, how did you see that I saved you from the man?” Then Abu Bakr asked for permission after that. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Aisha reconciled, and he said: Bring me into peace, just as you brought me into war, so the Messenger of God said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “We have done it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8815","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: I am Ali and he is Ibn Mushar, on the authority of Hashim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “Indeed, I know when you are satisfied with me, and when you are angry with me.” I said: What do you know, O Messenger of God? He said: “When you were angry with me and you swore, you said: No, by the Lord of Abraham, and if you were satisfied with me, you said: No, by the Lord of Muhammad.” I said: You are right, O Messenger of God. I only shun your name. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8816","Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-A'la informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Thawr narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Thawr, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said: I had been eager to ask 'Umar ibn al-Khattab about the two wives of the Prophet, peace be upon him, concerning whom Allah, the Most High, said: \If you two repent to Allah"","" then your hearts have inclined (to wrongdoing).\"" So 'Umar performed the Hajj"","" and I performed the Hajj with him. When we were on a part of the road"","" 'Umar turned aside"","" and I turned aside with him to a water-skin. He relieved himself"","" then came to me"","" and I poured water over his hands"","" and he performed wudu'. I said: \""O Commander of the Faithful"","" who are the two wives of the Prophet"","" peace be upon him"","" concerning whom Allah"","" the Mighty and Majestic"","" said to them: 'If you two repent to Allah"","" then your hearts have inclined'?\"" 'Umar said: \""How astonishing of you"","" O Ibn 'Abbas! 'A'ishah and Hafsah.\"" Then he took up the narration of the hadith. He said: We"","" the people of Quraysh"","" were a people who dominated women"","" but when we came to Madinah"","" we found a people whose women dominated them. So our women began to learn from their women. He said: My dwelling was in Banu Umayyah ibn al-Zayd in the 'Awali. One day I became angry with my wife"","" and lo"","" she was answering me back. I found it objectionable that she should answer me back. She said: \""What prevents you from answering me back? By Allah"","" the wives of the Prophet"","" peace be upon him"","" indeed answer him back"","" and one of them may boycott him from day to night.\"" I went off and entered upon Hafsah and said: \""Do you answer the Messenger of Allah"","" peace be upon him"","" back?\"" She said: \""Yes.\"" I said: \""And does one of you boycott him from day to night?\"" She said: \""Yes.\"" I said: \""She who does that among you has failed and perished. Does one of you feel secure that Allah may become angry with her for the anger of His Messenger"","" peace be upon him? If so"","" she has perished! Do not answer the Messenger of Allah"","" peace be upon him"","" back"","" and do not ask him for anything. Ask me whatever you wish"","" and let it not deceive you that your companion—meaning 'A'ishah—is more beautiful and more beloved to the Messenger of Allah"","" peace be upon him"","" than you.\"" I had a neighbour from the Ansar"","" and we used to take turns visiting the Messenger of Allah"","" peace be upon him. I would descend one day"","" and he would descend one day. He would bring me the news of the revelation and other matters"","" and I would bring him the like of that. We used to say that Ghassan was shoeing the horses to raid us. One day my companion descended"","" then came to me in the evening and knocked on my door"","" then called out. I went out to him and he said: \""A great event has occurred.\"" I said: \""What has happened? Have Ghassan come?\"" He said: \""No"","" but greater than that—the Prophet"","" peace be upon him"","" has divorced his wives.\"" I said: \""Hafsah has failed and perished! I had been thinking this would come to pass.\"" Until when I had prayed the morning prayer"","" I tightened my garments"","" then went down and entered upon Hafsah"","" and she was weeping. I said—then he mentioned a word to the meaning of: \""Has the Messenger of Allah"","" peace be upon him"","" divorced you?\"" She said: \""I do not know. He is in this chamber"","" secluded.\"" I met a black slave of his and said: \""Seek permission for 'Umar.\"" The slave entered"","" then came out to me and said: \""I have mentioned you to him"","" and he was silent.\"" I set out until I came to the minbar"","" and lo"","" there was a group of people sitting with him"","" some of them weeping. I sat for a while"","" but what I felt overcame me. I went to the slave and said: \""Seek permission for 'Umar.\"" The slave entered"","" then came back to me and said: \""I have mentioned you to him"","" and he was silent.\"" I sat by the minbar"","" but what I felt overcame me. I went back to the slave and said: \""Seek permission for 'Umar.\"" He entered"","" then came out"","" then came out to me and said: \""I have mentioned you"","" and he was silent.\"" I turned to leave"","" and lo"","" the slave was calling me"","" saying: \""Enter"","" for he has given you permission.\"" I entered and offered salam to the Messenger of Allah"","" peace be upon him. He was reclining upon a mat"","" which had left a mark on his side. I said: \""Have you divorced your wives"","" O Messenger of Allah?\"" He raised his head to me and said: \""No.\"" I said: \""Allahu Akbar! If you could see us"","" O Messenger of Allah—we"","" the people of Quraysh"","" were a people who dominated women"","" but when we came to Madinah"","" we found a people whose women dominated them. So our women began to learn from their women. I became angry with my wife"","" and she began to answer me back. I found it objectionable that she should answer me back. She said: 'What prevents you from answering me back? By Allah"","" the wives of the Prophet"","" peace be upon him"","" indeed answer him back"","" and one of them may boycott him from day to night.' I said: 'She who does that among you has failed and perished. Does one of you feel secure that Allah may become angry with her for the anger of His Messenger"","" peace be upon him? If so"","" she has perished!'\"" The Messenger of Allah"","" peace be upon him"","" smiled. I said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" I entered upon Hafsah and said: 'Let it not deceive you that your companion is more beautiful than you and more beloved to the Messenger of Allah"","" peace be upon him than you.'\"" He smiled again. I said: \""May I be at ease"","" O Messenger of Allah?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" So I sat"","" and I raised my head in the room. By Allah"","" I saw nothing in it to catch the eye except three hides. I said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" supplicate to Allah to provide for your Ummah"","" for He has provided for the Persians and the Romans"","" and they do not worship Allah.\"" He sat up straight and said: \""Are you in doubt"","" O son of al-Khattab? Those are a people whose good things were hastened for them in the life of this world.\"" I said: \""Seek forgiveness for me"","" O Messenger of Allah.\"" He said: And he had sworn that he would not enter upon them for a month"","" out of the intensity of his anger at them"","" when Allah"","" the Mighty and Majestic"","" had rebuked him."""""
"8817","Yusuf bin Saeed told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Yahya bin Abdullah bin Saifi told me that Ikrimah bin Abd al-Rahman bin al-Harith told him that Umm Salamah told him that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, swore that he would not enter some of his family for a month. When twenty-nine days had passed, he went to them tomorrow, and it was said to him: You swore not to enter upon them for a month. He said: “The month will be nine.” And twenty days.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8818","Yusuf bin Saeed told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abu al-Zubayr told me that he heard Jabir, saying: The Messenger retired God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, accompanied his wives for a month, so he went out on the morning of the twenty-nine, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Indeed, the month will be nine.” And twenty.” Then the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, clapped his hands three times: twice with all the fingers of his hand, and the third time with the nine of them. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8819","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Bahz, he said: my father told me, on the authority of my grandfather, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, our women What do we get from it, or what do we leave? He said: “You may cultivate it however you wish, except that you do not make an ugly face or hit her, and feed her when you feed her, and clothe her when you clothe yourself, and do not She should abandon her except in her home. How can you, when some of you have done harm to one another, except with what has been permissible for her? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8820","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: We are Shababah, he said: We are Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “There is no migration for more than three days, and whoever migrates for more than three days and dies, he will enter Hell.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8821","Muhammad bin Khalaf told us, he said: Adam told us, he said: Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah told us, he said: Thabit Al-Bunani told us, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: Safiyya was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey. That was that day. I slowed down on my way, and the Messenger of God met her. She was crying and saying: You carried me on a slow camel, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, started wiping her eyes with his hands. And he silenced her, but she refused to do anything except cry, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, became angry and left her. So I came and came to Aisha and said: My day. This is for you from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, if you please him with me. So Aisha went to her veil and dyed it. Boris and saffron, so she sprinkled some water on it, then came and sat at the head of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said to her: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “What’s wrong with you?” She said: That is God’s bounty. He gives it to whom He wills. So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, knew Hadith, he was satisfied with Safiyya, and went to Zainab and said to her: “Safiya has become exhausted with her camel, so what do you have to give her?” “Your camel,” Zainab said: “Should you go to my camel and give it to Judaism?” So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, emigrated to her for three months, and did not approach her home, and Zainab became idle and was idle in her home. She went to the bed, propped it towards the back of the house, and hoped that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would come to her. One day, when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, felt something, he entered the house and put the bed in its place, and Zainab said: O Messenger of God, My maid so-and-so has purified herself from her menstruation today. She is yours. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon her and was pleased with her. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8822","Muhammad bin Nasr told us, he said: Ayoub bin Sulayman told us, he said: Abu Bakr told me, on the authority of Sulayman, on the authority of Muhammad, and Musa, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, that Aisha said: “By God, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, never struck a woman of his with his hand.” He has never had a servant, nor has he ever touched anything with his hand, unless he strives in the path of God, and he has never been given a choice between two matters except that he chooses the easier of the two, unless He will be a sinner, for if it is a sin, he will be the furthest away from people, and by God, he never avenges himself for anything that is ever brought to him, until he has violated the sacred things. God will avenge God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8823","Abu Bakr bin Ali told me, he said: Ismail bin Ibrahim told me, he said: Ali bin Hashim told me, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Bakr Ibn Wa’il, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, never struck his wife, nor did he He has never flogged any of his servants, nor has he ever struck anything with his hand, unless in the cause of God, or the prohibitions of God were violated, so he could avenge God.”"
"8824","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Abdah, and Waki’, they said: Hisham bin Urwa told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “ I never saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, hit any of his servants, nor a woman, nor did he ever hit anything with his hand.” Abdah added: “Unless He strives in the cause of God.”"
"8825","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: I heard Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zam’a, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, exhorted them regarding the wind that was coming out. He said: “And why does any of you laugh at what comes from it?” And he exhorted them regarding women, “that “One of them strikes his wife as he strikes a male or female slave at the beginning of the day, then he hugs her at the end of the day.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8826","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Iyas bin Abdullah Ibn Abi Dhubab said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not strike God’s female slaves.” Then Omar came and said: The women have warned against Their wives, so he gave them permission, and they beat them. Then many women went around the family of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: And peace be upon him: “Tonight, seventy women went around the family of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, all of them complaining about their husbands, but we do not find them.” \Your choice\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"8827","Ishaq bin Mansour and Amr bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Al-Musli, on the authority of Al-Ash’ath ibn Qays, on the authority of Omar ibn Al-Khattab, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A man should not be asked while he struck his wife.”"
"8828","Ahmad bin Suleiman told us, he said: Husayn bin Ali, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Shabib bin Gharqada, on the authority of Suleiman bin Amr bin Al-Ahwas said: My father told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Treat women well, for they are your helpers. You shall not have the right to do anything from them other than that, unless they commit a clear indecency. If they do, then leave them to their beds and beat them. A beating that is not painful, so if they stab you, do not seek a way against them, except that you have a right from your wives, and your women have a right over you. Your right over your wives: let not those whom you dislike put on your beds, and let not those whom you dislike enter your homes, unless their right upon you is that you do good. To them in their clothing and food.”"
"8829","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Abu Usama told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Asma, she said: Al-Zubair married me, and he had no property on earth, nor any property, nor anything except his horse, so I used to feed his horse and provide him with his supplies. I ground it, and I use the finest kernels to freshen it, and I feed it, and I draw water, and I dig out its roots, and I knead, but I was not good at baking. My Ansar neighbors used to bake bread, and they were the women of Sadq, and I used to transport the stones from the land of Al-Zubayr, which were the ones that the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, cut. May God bless him and grant him peace, on my head, two-thirds of a farsakh, so I came one day, with the stones on my head, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, met me, and with him a group of His companions, so he called me, then said: “Akh, akh,” to carry me behind him, so I was ashamed to walk with the men, and I mentioned Al-Zubayr and his jealousy. He was one of the most jealous people, so the Messenger of God knew that I had become shy, so he went on, so I came to Al-Zubayr, and I said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, met me. He greeted me, with the stones on my head, and a group of his companions with him, so he called for me to ride with him. I was ashamed, and I recognized your jealousy. He said: “By God, It was more difficult for you to carry the palm trees than for you to ride with him.” She said: “Until Abu Bakr sent me after that a servant, and the Persian policy was enough for me. It is as if he had freed me.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8830","Abdah bin Abdullah told us, he said: I am Yazid, he said: I am Shu`bah, on the authority of Abu Qaza’ah, on the authority of Hakim bin Muawiyah, on the authority of his father, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, a man asked him: What is a woman’s right over her husband? He said: “You feed her when you feed her, and you clothe her when you clothe her, and you do not strike her in the face, and you do not curse her, and you do not leave her except in the house.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8831","Ziyad bin Yahya told us, he said: Azhar bin Saad, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ali, he said: Fatima complained to me about how much flour she had on her hands, so I said: If you went to your father and asked him for a servant, then she went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he did not She met him and returned. When he came, she was informed. He came to us and we had taken our beds, wearing velour. When we wore it for a long time, it came out of it. Our south, and when we wore it casually, our heads or feet would come out. He said: “O Fatima, I was told that you came. Was it Do you have anything to do?” I said: “Yes.” She complained to me about the amount of flour she had on her hand, and I said: “If you went to your father and asked a servant, he said: “Shall I not guide you?” What is better for you than a servant? When you go to your bed, say: thirty-three, thirty-three, and thirty-four: of praise. “And glorification and glorification.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8832","Yahya bin Uthman told us, he said: Na Baqiya, on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, He heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Every shepherd is responsible for his flock: the imam is a shepherd and responsible for his flock, and the man A shepherd among his family, and he is responsible for his flock, and a woman is a shepherd in her husband’s house, and she is responsible for her flock, and a servant A shepherd of his master’s property, and responsible for his flock, and a man is a shepherd of his father’s property, and he is responsible for his flock. Each of you is a shepherd, and each of you is a shepherd. “responsible for his flock”"
"8833","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Muadh bin Hisham, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “God will ask every shepherd about what he has kept. Did he preserve it or was it lost? Even a man will be asked about his household.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: No one we know narrated this on the authority of Muadh bin Hisham, except Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Rahawayh. Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Muadh bin Hisham, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, the same. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8834","Muhammad bin Al-Ala informed us, he said: Abu Bakr told us, he said: Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Wahb bin Jabir, he said: Abdullah bin Amr said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “It is enough sin for a man to neglect those he supports.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8835","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: I heard Sufyan, he said: Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Wahb bin Jabir, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Amr, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is enough sin for a man to waste what he provides for.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8836","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Al-Mu’tamir told us, he said: I read on Fudayl, on the authority of Abu Hariz, that Amr bin Abdullah Al-Hamdani, who is Abu Ishaq Al-Subai’i, narrated to him that Wahb bin Jabir Al-Khaywani narrated to him, that Abdullah bin Amr said: I heard the Prophet God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: “It is enough sin for a servant to waste what he provides for.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8837","Muhammad bin Nasr told us, he said: Ayoub bin Sulayman bin Bilal told us, he said: Abu Bakr told me, on the authority of Sulayman, on the authority of Muawiyah, and he Ibn Abi Al-Muzrid, on the authority of Abu Al-Hubab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is not a day when the servants wake up in the morning.” In it there is only two angels who say, and one of them says: O God, give the spender successor, and the other says: O God, give the one who takes possession of corruption. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8838","Ibrahim bin Harun told me, he said: Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, he said: Jafar bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of his father, he said: We entered upon Jabir bin Abdullah, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, addressed the people, and he said: “Fear God regarding women, for you have taken them in trust.” God, and you have made their private parts permissible with the word of God, and it is your duty that they should not put on your bed anyone whom you dislike, so if they do, then strike them. A beating that is not painful, and you are responsible for their provision, and you clothe them with kindness.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8839","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ali bin Nufayl told me, he said: Zuhayr told us, he said: Muhammad bin Jahadah told me, he said: Al-Hajjaj al-Bahili told me, he said: Suwayd bin Hujayr told me, on the authority of Hakim bin Muawiyah, on the authority of his father, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, what is true? Our wives are against us? He said: “Feed when you are fed, and clothe yourself when you are clothed, and do not strike your face, do not curse yourself, and do not forsake except at home.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8840","Qutaibah bin Sa’id told us, he said: Ya’qub told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He ordered to give charity, then a man came and said: Do I have a dinar? He said: “Spend it on yourself.” He said: Do I have another? He said: “Spend it on your wife.” He said: Do I have another? He said: “Spend it on your child.” He said: Do I have another? He said: “Spend it on your servant.” He said: Do I have another? He said: “You can see.”"
"8841","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Na Hammad, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of Abu Asma, on the authority of Thawban, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “The best dinar is a dinar that a man spends on his family, a dinar that a man spends on his animal in the path of God, and a dinar that a man spends on against his companions for the sake of God.” Abu Qalaba said: He started with the dependents. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8842","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muzahim bin Zufar, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Spend a dinar in the way of God, and a dinar for the needy, and a dinar for your family, and a dinar for freeing slaves, and a dinar for... Yahya forgot it, the best of them is a dinar: a dinar that you spent on your family.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8843","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Abdullah bin Maslamah told us, he said: Hatem told us, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Amr, on the authority of Al-Zabarqan bin Abdullah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Amr bin Umayyah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Everything you do for your family, it is It is a charity on them.” Brief"
"8844","Amr bin Uthman informed us, saying: Na Baqiya, on the authority of Buhair, on the authority of Khalid bin Ma’dan, on the authority of Al-Miqdam bin Ma’di Yakarib, that He heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whatever you feed yourself is charity for you, and whatever you feed your child is charity for you. “If you feed your wife, it is charity for you, and whatever you feed your servant, it is charity for you.”"
"8845","Amr bin Uthman bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Aamir bin Sa’d, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Indeed, God willing, you will not spend anything without being rewarded, until the morsel you raise to your wife’s mouth.”"
"8846","Saeed bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Malik bin Aws, he said: I heard Omar, He said: The wealth of Banu al-Nadir was from what God had given to His Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace, and for which the Muslims did not pay horses or riders. So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “would set aside the maintenance of his family for a year, then put what was left on his armor and weapons for the sake of God.”"
"8847","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Malik bin Aws bin Al-Hadathan, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Khattab, he said: The wealth of Banu al-Nadir was from what God had bestowed upon His Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace, which the Muslims did not pay miserly to. And no saddlebags, so he used to spend a year’s worth of it on his family, and whatever remained he put it on his weapons and saddlebags as equipment for the sake of God.”"
"8848","Ziyad bin Ayyub told us, he said: Sufyan, on the authority of Amr, and Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Malik bin Aws bin Al-Hadathan, on the authority of Omar, the wealth of Banu al-Nadir is among what God has given to His Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace, and for which the Muslims did not pay horses or passengers. It belonged to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sincerely, and he used to spend a year’s worth of it on his family, and of what remained he put on his armor and weapons as a number of supplies. “For the sake of God.”"
"8849","I am Muhammad bin Rafi’, he said: We are Abdul Razzaq, he said: I am Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, she said: Hind came to The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she said: O Messenger of God, Abu Sufyan is a constipated man, so is it a sin for me to spend on his family from His money, without his permission, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no blame on you if you spend on them in a reasonable manner.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8850","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Hisham, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Aisha, that Hind bint Utba, She said: O Messenger of God, Abu Sufyan is a stingy man, and he does not give me what is sufficient for me and my children, except what I take from him, and he does not know? He said: “Take what is sufficient for you and your child on a reasonable basis.”"
"8851","Abdul Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam told us, he said: Affan told us, he said: Wahib told us, he said: Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Asma She said: I said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: I do not own anything except what Al-Zubair brought me into his house, so should I take from his money? He said: “Spend, and do not neglect it, for it will be too late for you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8852","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, Ibn Jurayj said: Ibn Abi Mulaika told me, on the authority of Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr. On the authority of Asma’ bint Abu Bakr, she came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Prophet of God, I have nothing to do except what has been brought upon me. Al-Zubair, is it wrong for me to submit to what comes upon me? He said: “Be content as much as you can, and do not despair, for God will help you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8853","Hanad bin Al-Sirri told us, he said: Na Abda, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Fatima, on the authority of Asma, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said To her: “Do not count, then God will count for you.”"
"8854","Ahmad bin Harb told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Fatima, and Abbad bin Hamza, on the authority of Asma, she said: he said The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Spend, and do not be generous, and God will provide for you. Do not spend, and God will provide for you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8855","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna and Muhammad bin Bashar informed us, saying: Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, saying: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, saying: I heard Abu Wael narrated, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “If a woman gives alms from her husband’s house, she will have A reward, and the husband has the same, and the treasurer has the same, and each of them does not diminish the reward of its owner in the slightest: the husband gets what he earned. And what she spent is hers.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8856","Muhammad bin Qudamah told me, he said: Jarir told me, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “If a woman spends some of the food in her household without spoiling it, she will have a reward for what she spent, and the husband will have his reward for what Earning, and the treasurer has the same, and the reward of one of them does not diminish the reward of the other.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8857","Ahmad ibn Harb told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “If a woman spends from her husband’s house without spoiling it, she will have her reward, and he will have the same amount for what he earned. “And she will get what she spent, and the treasurer will have the same, without their wages being diminished in the slightest.”"
"8858","Yusuf bin Saeed told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, Abu Al-Zubayr told me, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Masruq, On the authority of Aisha, she said: “As long as a woman gives in charity from her household, the reward between them is two halves.”"
"8859","Hanad bin Al-Sirri and Muhammad bin Al-Ala told us, and the wording for it, they said: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Amr. Ibn Al-Harith Ibn Al-Mustaliq, on the authority of my nephew Zainab, the wife of Abdullah, on the authority of Zainab, the wife of Abdullah, she said: The Messenger of God addressed us May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: “O women, give in charity, even if it is your jewellery, for most of you will be the dwellers of Hell on the Day of Resurrection.” She said: Abdullah was a light man with a light hand, so I said to him: Ask the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, whether it is sufficient for me as part of charity to spend on My husband and orphans in my care? She said: And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was feared, so he said: No, rather ask him. She said: So I set off. So I came to the door, and behold, at the door was a woman from the Ansar, who was called: Zainab, her need is my need, so Bilal came out to us, so we said To him: Ask the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, for us: Is it sufficient for us in charity to spend on our wives and orphans in our homes? She said: Then Bilal entered and said to him: At the door is Zainab. He said: “Which Zainab?” He said: Zainab is Abdullah’s wife, and Zainab is a woman. From the Ansar, they ask you about spending on their wives and orphans in their homes. This suffices for them as charity, so the Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “They have two rewards: the reward of kinship, and the reward of charity.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8860","Bishr bin Khalid Al-Askari told us, he said: We are Ghandar, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Sulayman, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith, On the authority of Zainab, the wife of Abdullah, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to the women: “Give in charity, even if it is from your adornments.” She said: And it was Abdullah is light-handed, so she said to him: Can I give my charity to you, and to my brother’s children who are orphans? Abdullah said: Ask the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about that. She said: So I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and behold, at his door A woman from the Ansar, called Zainab, was asking about what I was asking about. Then Bilal came out to us, and I said to him: Go to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, so ask him about that, and do not tell him who we are. So he went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Who are they?” He said: Zainab. He said: Which Zaynab? He said: Zainab, the wife of Abdullah and Zainab al-Ansariyya. He said: Yes, she has two rewards: a reward. kinship, and the reward of charity.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8861","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Omar bin Hafs bin Ghayath told me, he said: my father told me, he said: Al-A’mash told me, he said: a brother told me, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Zainab, Abdullah’s wife, so she mentioned him to Ibrahim, and he told me I see him, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Zainab, Abdullah’s wife, and similarly, she said: I was in the mosque, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw me. He said: “Give in charity, even if it is from your jewellery.” Zainab was spending on Abdullah and orphans in her family, so she said to Abdullah: Is that sufficient? Am I supposed to spend on you, and on the orphans in my care, from charity? He said: Ask the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So I went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and found a woman from the Ansar on the Her need is the same as mine, so Bilal passed by us and we said: Ask the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Is it sufficient for me to spend on My husband and orphans in my care from charity? So he went in and asked him, and he said: “Who are they?” He said: Zainab. He said: “Which Zaynab?” He said: Abdullah’s wife. He said: “Yes, it will be hers.” Two rewards: the reward of kinship, and the reward of charity.”"
"8862","Al-Qasim bin Zakaria informed us, saying: I am Ubayd Allah bin Musa, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Ibrahim, meaning the son of an immigrant, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, said: Abdullah’s wife and Ibn Masoud’s wife went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, each One woman kept her friend secret, so they came to the room and said to Bilal: Come to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and say: Two women. One of them has surplus money, and in her custody are the sons of a brother who has orphans? The other woman said: I have an abundance of wealth, and I have a husband who is light-hearted? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “They have two guarantors.”"
"8863","Issa bin Ahmad Al-Asqalani informed me, in Balkh. He said: Na Baqiya. He said: Buhair bin Saad narrated to me, on the authority of Khalid bin Maadan, on the authority of Al-Miqdam bin Maadi Karib said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whatever you feed yourself is charity for you, and whatever you feed Your wife, it is charity for you, and whatever you feed your child, it is charity for you, and whatever you feed your servant, it is charity for you.”"
"8864","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Bishr bin al-Mufaddal told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid On the authority of Abu Masoud, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “When a Muslim spends on his family, while he expects it from it, “Sadaqah was recorded for him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8865","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Abd al-Razzaq, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Aamir bin Saad, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “O Sa’d, you will never spend an expense, seeking the pleasure of God, without being rewarded for it, even the morsel of food.” You put her in the mouth of your wife.”"
"8866","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Amer bin Saad, on the authority of his father, He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No matter how much you spend, it is charity, even a morsel that you raise to your wife’s mouth.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8867","Suleiman bin Ubaid Allah bin Amr told us. We wrote about him in Basra. He said: Abu Amer Abd al-Malik bin Amr told us. He said: Na. Zakaria bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, said: Abu Bakr came to ask permission to come to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And the people were sitting at its gate, but permission was not given to him, then Omar came and he asked for permission, but he was not given permission, so he sat down, then permission was given to Abu Bakr and Omar. So they entered and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was sitting, and his wives were around him, and he was very silent. Omar said: I will speak to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Perhaps he would laugh. Omar said: O Messenger of God, if you saw Zayd’s daughter, Omar’s wife, ask me for maintenance just now, so I bent her neck. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, laughed until his molars became visible. He said: “They are around me, as you can see. They are asking me for maintenance.” So Abu Bakr rose to Aisha to beat her, and Omar stood up to Hafsa, both of them saying: You are asking the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for what he does not have, so he forbade them both. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his wives said: By God, we will not ask the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, after this gathering something that is not Then God Almighty sent down the choice, starting with Aisha, and said: “I want to mention to you something that I do not like for you to rush into, so that You ask your parents for advice.” She said: What is it, O Messenger of God? So he recited to her: “O Prophet, tell your wives, ‘If you desire the life of this world and its adornments, then come, I will give you pleasure.’” Aisha said: “Is it okay with you?” Should I consult my parents? ! Rather, I choose God and His Messenger and the Hereafter, and I ask you not to mention to any of your wives what I have chosen. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “Indeed, God did not send me as a scolder, but as a teacher who brought good tidings of good news. No woman among them asks me what I have chosen unless I tell her.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8868","Muhammad bin Abdul Aziz bin Abi Rizmah told us, he said: Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The best charity is that which is done on the back of wealth, and the upper hand is better than the lower hand.” “Whom do you support?” The woman says: Either you spend on me, or you divorce me. The son says: To whom do you leave me? And the servant says: Spend on me. And employ me.” It was said: “O Abu Hurairah, is this on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace?” He said: No, this is from my sack. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8869","Imran bin Bakkar told me, he said: I am Al-Rabi’ bin Ruh, he said: we are Mughirah bin Abdul Rahman, he said: we are Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Zaid bin Aslam, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “The upper hand is better than the lower hand.” “Whom do you support?” Zaid said: Abu Hurairah was asked: Who do you depend on, Abu Hurairah? He said: Your wife, she says: Spend on me, or divorce me, and your servant says: Feed me and use me, and your son says: To whom will you leave me? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8870","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid told us, he said: My father told us, he said: Saeed told us, he said: Ibn Ajlan told me, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Abu Saleh, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The best charity is that which is done from the appearance of wealth, and a high hand is better than The lower hand, and start with whom you support.” It was said: Who do I support, O Messenger of God? He said: “Your wife is one of your dependents. She says: Feed me, otherwise you will leave me. Your servant says: Feed me and employ me. And your son says: To whom? Are you leaving me? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8871","Qutaibah told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No.” “A woman asks for a divorce from her sister, so that she can empty her family and get married, for she only gets what has been decreed for her.”"
"8872","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Abdullah told me, he said: Bishr bin Shuaib told me, he said: my father told me, on the authority of al-Zuhri, he said: Abu told me Salamah, and Saeed, that Abu Hurairah said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “A woman should not ask for another woman’s divorce in order to be satisfied with it.” whatever is in its vessel” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8873","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Muawiyah bin Hisham, he said: Ammar bin Ruzaiq told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Isa bin Abdul Al-Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Yahya bin Yamar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Who “Whoever turns a slave against his family is not one of us, and whoever spoils a woman against her husband is not one of us.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8874","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: I am Hushaym, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Doesn’t he spend the night? A man with a woman, unless he is a married man or a mahram.”"
"8875","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Abu Al-Khair, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, that the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Beware of entering upon women.” Then a man from the Ansar said: Have you seen the mother-in-law? He said: “The father-in-law: death.”"
"8876","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: I am Ibn Wahb, he said: Amr bin Al-Harith told me, that Bakr bin Sawada told him, that Abd al-Rahman bin Jubair told him that Abdullah bin Amr bin al-Aas told him that a group of Banu Hashim entered upon Asma’ bint Umays, so Abu Bakr entered, and she was under him at that time. He disliked that, so he mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “I I saw nothing but good.” He said: “God has exonerated her from that.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up on the pulpit and said: “They shall not enter.” A man will remain absent after this day of mine, unless one or two men are with him.”"
"8877","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Abu Ma’bad, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, And he said: “A man should not be alone with a woman.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8878","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Jarir, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra, he said: Omar proposed to the tax collector. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood in a position similar to this, then he said: “Do good to my companions, then those who come after them. Then those who follow them, then they spread lies, to the point that a man swears an oath before he is sworn to it, and bears witness to martyrdom before being cited as a martyr. Whoever among you wants to attain the reward of Paradise should adhere to the group, for Satan is with The one, which is further from the two, is that no man should be alone with a woman, for the third of them is Satan. And whoever of you is distressed by it. His bad deed, or his good deed pleases him, then he is a believer.” Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Wahb bin Jarir bin Hazim, he said: my father told us, he said: I heard Abd al-Malik bin Umair speaking, On the authority of Jabir bin Samurah, he said: Omar addressed us in the Jabiya, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rose among us, and he mentioned something similar to the hadith of Jarir."
"8879","Abdullah bin Al-Sabbah bin Abdullah told us, he said: Abdul-A’la bin Abdul-A’la told us, he said: Hisham, who is Ibn Hassan, told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra, said: Omar addressed us with the tax collector, and said: A messenger has risen among us. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, is my position among you today, and he said: “Do good to my companions, then those who follow them, then the lie spreads, until When a man bears witness, he does not ask her about it, and until he takes an oath, he does not ask about it. So whoever wants to attain Paradise, let him adhere to the group. Satan is with the one, and he is further away from the two. Do not let any of you be alone with a woman, for Satan is the third of them, and who “His good deeds please him, and his bad deeds displease him, so he is a believer.”"
"8880","Quraysh ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Baroudi informed us, he said: Ali ibn al-Hasan, he said: I am al-Husayn ibn Waqid, he said: we are Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, who said: I heard Ibn al-Zubayr, saying: I heard Omar ibn al-Khattab giving a sermon, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, giving a sermon. So he said: “Honor my companions, then those after them, then those after them, then lies appear, until a man testifies and is not martyred. And the man swears, but he is not made to swear. Whoever among you loves the reward of Paradise, let him adhere to the group, for Satan is with one, and he is Farther from the two than the two, and never let a man be alone with a woman, for the third of them is Satan, and whoever is pleased with him is good, and whose evil is unpleasant to him. He is a believer.”"
"8881","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told me, he said: Hajjaj bin Muhammad told me, he said: Yunus bin Abi Ishaq told me, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Zubair, who said: The Commander of the Faithful, Omar, rose among us at the gate of the tax collectorate, and said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rose among us. Like my standing among you, and he said: “O people, honor my companions, then those next to them, then those next to them, then the lie spreads, until A man swears before he is sworn, and bears witness before he is martyred, so whoever is pleased to attain the reward of Paradise must do so. With the group, for the hand of God is over the group. No man will be alone with a woman, for Satan is the third of them. Indeed, Satan is with one And it is further from the two. Except for him whose evil deeds displeases him and whose good deeds please him, that is the believer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8882","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, he said: Ishaq bin Bakr told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abdullah bin A dinar, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that when Omar ibn al-Khattab came to the Levant, he stood up and said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rose up among us as I have risen. among you, and he said: “Honor my companions, then those next to them, then those next to them, then the lie appeared, so the man swears and does not swear.” And he will bear witness but not be martyred. Whoever wants to be rewarded with Paradise must adhere to the group, for Satan is with the one who excels, and he is farther away from the two. “And a man should not be alone with a woman who is not permissible for him, for Satan is the third of them.”"
"8883","Muhammad bin Al-Walid told us, he said: Al-Nadr bin Ismail told us, he said: Muhammad bin Suqa told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Omar, he said: Omar addressed us with the jabiya, and he said: I stand among you as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood among us, so he said: “I advise you My companions, then those next to them, then the lie is spread, until a man swears an oath and is not sworn, and until he bears witness and is not cited as a martyr, upon you. With the group, and beware of separation, for Satan is with the one, and he is further away from the two. A man will never be alone with a woman, three bitter, unless the third of them is a devil. Whoever wants to enter Paradise, let him adhere to the group. Whoever is pleased with it is its good, and its evil displeases him. That is the believer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8884","Safwan bin Amr told us, he said: Musa bin Ayyub told us, he said: Ata bin Muslim told us, he said: Muhammad bin Suqa told us, on the authority of Abu Salih, He said: Omar presented the collector and said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Guard me among my companions, then those next to them, three Several times, then a people will come after that who will bear witness without being asked for martyrdom, and swear without being asked to swear, so whoever loves Paradise, so he must do so in company, for Satan is near to the one, and far from the two, and no man is alone with a woman unless he is Muharram, and whoever is pleased with his good deeds, and whose evil deeds displeases him, is a believer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8885","Ubaid Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim told us, he said: My uncle told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Nabhan is the servant of Umm Salamah told him that Umm Salamah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had made a covenant with us: “If one of us has offices, So he completed what remained of his writing, so cover the veil without it.” Ubayd Allah ibn Saad told me about it in another place, and he said: “If the office has something to pay for, then hide from it.”"
"8886","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: We heard it from Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Nabhan, he said: Umm Salamah said to me: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: “If one of you has offices, and he has something to give, then you should veil yourself from him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8887","Harun bin Abdullah told me, he said: I am Ibn Abi Fudaik, he said: I am Al-Dahhak bin Uthman, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Ibn Abi Saeed Al-Khudri, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A man should not look at a man’s nakedness, and you should not look at a man’s nakedness.” “A woman is exposed to a woman’s nakedness, and a man does not open to a man in clothing, and a woman does not open to a woman in clothing.”"
"8888","Ibrahim bin Yusuf Al-Balkhi told me, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told me, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: “The Prophet forbade God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, has enjoined that a woman be clothed in the same garment, in order that she may describe it to her husband.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8889","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told me, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour. H and Issa bin Yunus, on the authority of Al-A’mash, both on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “A woman should not have sexual intercourse with The woman describes her to her husband as if he were looking at her.”"
"8890","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Ubayd Allah is ours, he said: I am Israel, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah He said: “A woman should not have intercourse with another woman, nor should a man have intercourse with another man.”"
"8891","Imran bin Musa told us, he said: Abdul-Warith told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Amr bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah, on the authority of Jarir, he said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about the sudden look. He said: “Lower your gaze.”"
"8892","Ahmad bin Saeed told me, he said: Wahb bin Jarir told me, he said: Qurrah bin Khaled told me, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid bin Jubayr, on the authority of his paternal aunt. Safiya bint Shaybah said: Aisha told us, she said: I said: O Messenger of God, people return with two sacrifices, and I return with one sacrifice? ! So Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr ordered me to go to al-Tan`im, and he sent me behind him on a camel, on a very hot night, and I was leaving my veil behind me. My neck, then he grabbed my leg and hit it with the palm of his hand. I said: Do you see anyone? So we ended at Tan'im, and I performed Ihram for Umrah from there, so I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was in Batha and did not leave. That was the day of the battle, so I said: O Messenger of God, should I not enter the house? He said: “Enter the stone, for it is from the house.”"
"8893","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told me, he said: Shuaib bin Al-Layth told me, on the authority of his father, he said: Sa’id bin Abdul Rahman Al-Jumahi told me, on the authority of my father Hazim, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad, said: “When it was the day of Uhud, and the polytheists had departed from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the women went out To the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his companions were following them by water. Fatima was among those who went out, and when she met the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, May God bless him and grant him peace, she embraced him and started washing his wound with water, so the blood increased. When she saw that, she took some of the mat. So she burned it with fire and compressed it until it stuck to the wound and the blood oozed out.”"
"8894","Zakaria bin Yahya informed me. He said: This is Ishaq. He said: I am Al-Nadr bin Shumail. He said: I am Israel. He said: I am Maysara bin Habib Al-Nahdi. He said: Al-Minhal bin Amr told me, he said: Aisha bint Talha told me, on the authority of Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, she said: I did not see anyone from People liken the words of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to a conversation or a session from Fatima. She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was If he saw her coming, he welcomed her, then he got up to her, kissed her, then took her hand and brought her so that he could make her sit in his place. And whenever she saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, she would welcome him, then she would get up to him and kiss him, and she would enter upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May peace and blessings be upon him during his illness in which he died. He welcomed her, kissed her, then confided in her, and she cried. Then he confided in her, and she laughed. So I said to the women: I only saw that she had superiority over the women, so behold, she was one of the women, and while she was crying, she laughed! So I asked her, What did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say to you? She said: Then I am a seed. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was arrested, I asked her, and she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He greeted me and said: “My time has come, and I am dead.” So I cried. Then he said: “You are the first of my family to join me.” I was pleased, and he liked it. I laughed (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8895","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Othman bin Omar told us, he said: I am Israel, on the authority of Maysara bin Habib, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Aisha bint Talha, on the authority of Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, who said: I have never seen a woman whose speech and speech resemble those of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. From Fatima, and whenever she entered his house, he took her by the hand, kissed her, and made her sit in his seat, and whenever he entered upon her, She went up to him, kissed him, took his hand, and went in to see him during his illness in which he died. He confided in her, and she wept. Then he confided To her, and she laughed, so I said: I thought that this woman had superiority over women, so behold, she was one of them. While she was crying, behold, she You laugh! So I asked her, and she said: “Then I am a seed.” When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died, I asked her, and she said: “He confided to me He told me that he was dead, and I cried. Then he confided to me that I would be the first of his family to join him, and I laughed.”"
"8896","Muhammad bin Yahya informed us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “He did not touch The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, never touched a woman’s hand, except a woman he owned.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8897","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala informed us, he said: I am Ibn Wahb. He said: Yunus, who is Ibn Yazid al-Ayli, informed me. He said: Ibn Shihab said: Urwa bin Al-Zubayr told me that Aisha said: “No, by God, the hand of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, has never touched the hand of a woman. “Unless he pledges allegiance to them verbally.”"
"8898","Al-Harith bin Miskin, a reading of it, and I hear, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: I am Malik, on the authority of Muhammad bin al-Munkadir, on the authority of Umaima bint Raqiqa, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I do not shake hands with women.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8899","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: I am Ibn Wahb, he said: I am Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Nabhan, the client of Umm Salamah, he narrated to him, Umm Salamah told him that she was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and while we were with him, Ibn Umm Maktum came and entered. On him, and that was after he was commanded to wear the veil, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Hide yourself from him.” So we said: O Messenger of God, isn’t it? Is he blind? He cannot see us and does not know us. ! Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Are you both blind? Do you not see him?” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: We do not know of anyone who narrated on the authority of Nabhan other than al-Zuhri."
"8900","Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told me, he said: Saeed bin Abi Maryam told me, he said: Nafi bin Yazid told me, he said: Tell me Aqeel said: Ibn Shihab told me, on the authority of Nabhan, the client of Umm Salamah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon me. He greeted me, while Maimunah and I were sitting, so he sat down, and the blind Ibn Umm Maktoum asked permission for him, and he said: “Hide yourself from him.” We said: O Messenger of God, Is it not that we are blind and cannot see? ! He said: “Do you see it?!”"
"8901","Qutaibah told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Imran bin Abi Anas, on the authority of Abu Salamah, he said: I asked Fatima, daughter of Qays, and she told me Her husband, Al-Makhzoumi, divorced her, but he refused to spend on her, so she went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and told him, Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You are not entitled to maintenance, so go and go to Ibn Umm Maktum and be with him, for he is a blind man.” \You put your clothes on there.\"""""""
"8902","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abi al-Jahm, he said: I heard Fatima bint Qays, she said: My husband, Abu Amr ibn Hafs ibn al-Mughirah, sent me a letter to divorce me, and he sent me five o’clock Barley, and five asa’ of dates, so I said: What do I have other than this, and should I not observe the waiting period in your house? ! He said: No, so I tightened my clothes, then I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “How many times has he divorced you?” I said: Three times. He said: “He has spoken the truth, and you are not entitled to maintenance.” “Perform the waiting period in the house of your cousin, Ibn Umm Maktoum, for he is blind. Throw away your clothes. When your waiting period is over, then inform me.” Then a suitor from among them, Muawiyah and Abu al-Jahm, proposed to me, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “As for Muawiyah, he is poor and his condition is light. Abu Al-Jahm beats women, or he was harsh on women, but you should marry Usama bin Zaid,” or he said: “Marry Usama bin Zaid.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8903","Muhammad ibn Adam told me, on the authority of Abdah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Zainab bint Umm Salamah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, was with her, and in the house there was an effeminate man, and the effeminate man said to Umm Salamah’s brother, Abdullah bin Abi Umayyah: If God grants you victory over Taif Tomorrow, I will guide you to Bint Ghaylan, for she faces four times and turns eight. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “These people shall not enter.” \On you\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"8904","Nuh bin Habib told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Khalid, on the authority of Rabah bin Zayd, on the authority of Muammar, then he mentioned words that mean: on the authority of Al-Zuhri, On the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered and behold, some of his wives looked effeminate, and they were counting him as someone other than her. He was given the robe, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard him say: When she approaches, she approaches with four, and when she turns away, she turns away. With eight, he described a woman, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Do I not see that this person knows what is here? They do not enter upon you, so block him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8905","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Abdullah told us, he said: Abdul Razzaq told us, he said: I am Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, She said: There was a man who entered upon the wives of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he was effeminate, and they considered him to be someone who did not have decency, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered. peace be upon him, while he was with one of his wives, and he was describing a woman, and he said: When she comes, she comes four times, and when She turned away, turned away with eight, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do I not see that this person knows what is here? They will not enter upon you.” So they blocked him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8906","Hilal bin Al-Ala told me, he said: Al-Hajjaj bin Al-Minhal told me, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told me, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Omar bin Abi Salamah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered the house of Umm Salamah, who was with her, and she was effeminate, and he said: O Abdullah bin Abi Umayyah, if you had conquered Taif, I would have shown you Badia bint Ghaylan, for she faces four fronts and turns eight, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said. Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Do not let this enter upon you.”"
"8907","Ahmad ibn Harb told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Zainab, on the authority of Umm Salamah, she said: He entered upon her. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and with her was her brother Abdullah, and with her was an androgynous, and he was saying: O Abdullah, if God grants you victory Al-Taif, you should consider the daughter of Ghaylan, for she approaches with four and goes in with eight. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Umm Salamah: “They shall not enter.” \That's on you.\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"8908","Al-Harith bin Miskin read about it, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, who said: Malik told me, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, that he was an effeminate man. Umm Salamah, and he said to Abdullah bin Abi Umayyah, while the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was listening: O Abdullah, if God grants you victory over Taif tomorrow I will direct you to the daughter of Ghaylan, for she faces four times and goes backwards with eight. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “They shall not enter.” These are upon you.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: The hadith of Hisham is more likely to be authentic, and al-Zuhri is more reliable in Urwah than Hisham, and Hisham is more reliable than al-Haffaf. The hadith of Hammad bin Salamah is an error"
"8909","Muhammad bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Bishr, who is Ibn al-Mufaddal, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, he said: He told me Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “cursed effeminate men and effeminate women, and said: expel them from your homes.” So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, expelled so-and-so, and Omar expelled so-and-so. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8910","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna informed us, he said: I am Al-Walid bin Muslim, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Ikrimah, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace, “He brought out a hermaphrodite, and Omar brought out so-and-so and so-and-so.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
